{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>See, You say to me.</b> This is what they call this parashah on Shabbat of chol ha-moed, because the Sabbath is mentioned in it in the midst of the festivals, and in the megillah they read Rashi's commentary because there are commandments of Sabbath and festivals there. And an allusion to chol ha-moed, as it is written ״את חג המצות תשמור שבעת ימים״ — and they derived from here the prohibition of labor on chol ha-moed, in tractate Ḥagigah." "<b>[See, You say to me.</b> Set your mind to observe.]" "<b>And You have not made known to me.</b> For You said, ״ואדעה מה אעשה לך״, yet You did not reveal to me whether You will send an angel or whether You Yourself will go."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {0 "The megillah referred to is likely the megillah of the synagogue readings for the festivals. The phrase 'ובמגלה פרש״י' may mean 'and in the megillah they read Rashi' or refer to Rashi's commentary on the megillah."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:01:41.706062603Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}